{"title":"Kimberling’s point X(24)","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Kimberling&#39;s_point_X(24)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Kimberling's point X(24)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Theorem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Theorem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Theorem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Theorem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Theorem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Theorem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span id=\"Kimberling.27s_point_X.2824.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Kimberling's_point_X(24)\">Kimberling's point X(24)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Kimberling%E2%80%99s_point_X(24)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Kimberling&#39;s point X(24)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2016_USAMO_3g.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/0/06/2016_USAMO_3g.png/450px-2016_USAMO_3g.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"450\" height=\"335\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/0/06/2016_USAMO_3g.png/675px-2016_USAMO_3g.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/0/06/2016_USAMO_3g.png/900px-2016_USAMO_3g.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Kimberling defined point X(24) as perspector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and Orthic Triangle of the Orthic Triangle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Theorem_1\">Theorem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Kimberling%E2%80%99s_point_X(24)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Theorem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/0/6801c07694edb238c4a095956d8bf46ccdb38fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> obtuse or acute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/919b9f77a6985e760286799909be5bfe0152f40e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/0/6801c07694edb238c4a095956d8bf46ccdb38fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> be the base triangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/b/0abfcd62b575da480039a495ab1ab18f54e81632.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_1 = \\triangle DEF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" /> be Orthic triangle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/f/26fc6549cf9bd6f5b84d1ce793521696d3812052.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_0, T_2 = \\triangle UVW$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"18\" /> be Orthic Triangle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/7/c073f8a05257a19c2dacc368858763bb44fa3747.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the circumcenter and orthocenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/0/060b13a1e141783844c9df0e251553bd50eb1388.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> \n</p><p>Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/a/b0a8f65c364086b3b76ee0c21195835751ed0621.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle T_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/2/f927889d1f133d6b4b414a81fa7324631f3931d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle T_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> are homothetic, the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/e/ede78a06018011f48c24a76284afce482ebc6c47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" /> center of this homothety lies on Euler line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/b/e7b315b83c0b7c2f735f66c03cf870a83da077d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OH$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/0/060b13a1e141783844c9df0e251553bd50eb1388.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> \n</p><p>The ratio of the homothety is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/0/9d0878be6845f3525ff8d15329821a3232bd1e2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = \\frac {\\vec {PH}}{\\vec {OP}}= 4 \\cos A \\cos B \\cos C.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"242\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p><i><b>Proof</b></i> \n</p><p>WLOG, we use case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde544759d10090f3b9b1cec7ea569037be2353.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A = \\alpha &gt; 90^\\circ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"119\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c71f19552a05ee5e2b31e94aff3fb986884bf31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be reflection <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/3/883839dc660034eb7a3172ac925f7bce4bd9de34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE.$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> In accordance with Claim, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/2/9a2c3330041c3e24fc50263e0a401ff9e980f8fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BVD = \\angle HVE \\implies B&#39;, V,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"236\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are collinear.\n</p><p>Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/f/2df4a296d1c6eddb959715344b66077ae5d0b8ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C, W,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/c/d6cbc45cd93a2b17b17a9d035a45847271b55322.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C&#39;,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> were <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b798193cb94562989018728e1151587c618655b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"16\" /> is reflection <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/7/a373ea978487bdedfa6b8facca28e370808fce54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DF,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> are collinear.\n</p><p>Denote  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/1/b31412bd77d29a09b3e1eab76b57b69bd27d2b71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC = \\beta = \\angle CHD, \\angle ACB = \\gamma = \\angle BHD \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"403\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/e/d2ef26f8fb405398b72a59c78ed30bb87663f9c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle HDF = \\angle HDE = \\angle DHB&#39; = \\angle DHC&#39; = 180^\\circ - \\alpha.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"420\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/9675876d1741e6bb39654884e7abbd11be92e747.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;C&#39; \\perp HD, BC \\perp HD \\implies BC|| B&#39;C&#39;.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"322\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/b/69b46278d942ea186fd69d1e75e894d6bc16c04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OB = OC, HB&#39; = HC&#39;, \\angle BOC = \\angle B&#39;HC&#39; = 360^\\circ - 2 \\alpha \\implies OB ||HB&#39;, OC || HC&#39; \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"697\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/2/b82ff0dbdc5bf91a4e8d451c2af58beab3194984.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle HB&#39;C&#39; \\sim \\triangle OBC, BB&#39;, CC&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"239\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/b/d7b5d4cfb1c908ed6b63726f10da0814745d0668.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HO$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> are concurrent at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/c/e3ce33ec2a34dc4fddaec3224043f4a72bbe6d0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>In accordance with <i><b>Claim,</b></i> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/5/2358a72d05db61507546bab55c6215a4902d6978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle HUF = \\angle AUF \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"184\" height=\"14\" /> points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are isogonal conjugate with respect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/3/ea34d467509b6adaba0d6d83928125be7d5f4a37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle UVW.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" /> \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/4/d548da4e478b6f4f41e6a7c231bcbe3f15b75066.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle HDE = \\alpha - 90^\\circ, \\angle HCD = 90^\\circ - \\beta \\implies\\]\" width=\"332\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/2/3c2e2c01b781d5d20d3473040af85bbdf7c3e94e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[HB&#39; = 2 HD \\sin (\\alpha - 90^\\circ) = - 2 CD \\tan(90^\\circ- \\beta) \\cos \\alpha = - 2 AC \\cos \\gamma \\frac {\\cos \\beta}{\\sin \\beta} \\cos \\alpha = - 4 OB \\cos A \\cos B \\cos C.\\]\" width=\"820\" height=\"41\" />   \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/e/9fe990a312df1dacb7a220bf207d8e6ff755e7af.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k = \\frac {HB&#39;}{OB} = \\frac {HP}{OP}= - 4 \\cos A \\cos B \\cos C \\implies \\frac {\\vec {PH}}{\\vec {OP}}= 4 \\cos A \\cos B \\cos C.\\]\" width=\"568\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><i><b>Claim</b></i>\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2016_3_Lemma.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/97/2016_3_Lemma.png/400px-2016_3_Lemma.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"249\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/97/2016_3_Lemma.png/600px-2016_3_Lemma.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/97/2016_3_Lemma.png/800px-2016_3_Lemma.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> be an acute triangle, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/c/efc888ed14fcc394dcceed562a0efcf02333cf51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AH, BD&#39;,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> denote its altitudes. Lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/5/825000b887cf170e8a54ee5dcdafffbdfb959cea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DD&#39;$\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> meet at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/0/7b0db3a76cfe77eff9011a1e1f1c1d7c03186479.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q, HS \\perp DD&#39;.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"19\" /> Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/3/fe3a2013626874c16a8f23227b71751742554f57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BSH = \\angle CSH.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"142\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><i><b>Proof</b></i>\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> be the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/9/809fd1acfe31ef9694ca83991dbca90c7e53875e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCD&#39;D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"67\" height=\"16\" /> centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/e/d3e1b6d951642f21ac7ff29484d08b494f44a140.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O (O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> is midpoint <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/f/a6fe9deea8f3a5182b055f66c9cd9fc54ccd9132.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"43\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> meet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/3/bb3ddf9a5fa2fca5c4787d4f989af0eef1387bf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AH$\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/c/e3ce33ec2a34dc4fddaec3224043f4a72bbe6d0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> \nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> be the circle centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/7/1e70aa629d0d60924cbd420942e6785b46b8cba5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QP.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/2/a321d1b883ba985b1f59ca076beaaf17aa8ab06c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the circle with diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/2/262a086544e207829375d3029f95a823490cd4b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OQ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"32\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Well known that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/3/bb3ddf9a5fa2fca5c4787d4f989af0eef1387bf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AH$\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" /> is the polar of point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/4/5646f1d6eed76fee4840dacf4c8fb39ef64fe46e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"16\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/9/0e9640a10ce799c6ffcf747e715450a3f8fb6f8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QO \\cdot HO = QP^2 \\implies QB \\cdot QC = (QO – R) \\cdot (QO + R) = QP^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"498\" height=\"21\" />  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/7/29707a885ccd1f2f9e1cc0a0801c0b45e581edac.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies P \\in \\Theta,  \\Omega \\perp \\omega.\\]\" width=\"149\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/e/22ec107d9afef9af9ebb250e7321724484a3f482.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_{\\Omega}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> be inversion with respect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/4/9a44ad9a8462adfcae69d234577dccc3c6ba8550.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega, I_{\\Omega}(B) = C,  I_{\\Omega}(H) = O,I_{\\Omega}(D) = D&#39;.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"309\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67b7dcc7e5857672753ea51229d48a830fb0a5bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_{\\Omega}(S) = S&#39;.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"93\" height=\"20\" /> \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/9/4196e41638c70a058b927e08c28fd148ee523e68.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[HS \\perp DD&#39; \\implies S&#39;O \\perp BC \\implies BS&#39; = CS&#39; \\implies \\angle OCS&#39; = \\angle OBS&#39;.\\]\" width=\"553\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/7/ae7ddd134a33332e313781036b656f30798ec471.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle QSB = \\angle QCS&#39; = \\angle OCS&#39; = \\angle OBS&#39; = \\angle CSS&#39;.\\]\" width=\"386\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/6/88665d98ea5f235e3374eaa8d8cf14ae0967e541.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle BSH = 90 ^\\circ  – \\angle QSB = 90 ^\\circ  – \\angle CSS&#39; =\\angle CSH.\\]\" width=\"368\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Theorem_2\">Theorem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Kimberling%E2%80%99s_point_X(24)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Theorem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2016_USAMO_3e.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/b/b3/2016_USAMO_3e.png/400px-2016_USAMO_3e.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"462\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/b/b3/2016_USAMO_3e.png/600px-2016_USAMO_3e.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/b/b3/2016_USAMO_3e.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/0/d00f37c87885059f22bcc4f4353600456657bc3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_0 = \\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" /> be the base triangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/b/0abfcd62b575da480039a495ab1ab18f54e81632.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_1 = \\triangle DEF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" /> be orthic triangle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/3/c634a482a72eb46e9760e38b612c3e9752be92da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_0, T_2 = \\triangle KLM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"18\" /> be Kosnita triangle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/0/060b13a1e141783844c9df0e251553bd50eb1388.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/d/17db72a808094d4d7569b25b1184ac4c31e26dcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle T_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/2/f927889d1f133d6b4b414a81fa7324631f3931d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle T_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> are homothetic, the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/e/ede78a06018011f48c24a76284afce482ebc6c47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" /> center of this homothety lies on Euler line of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/a/50a41591fc926e02399a97608c4a03bb2fa03e57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"18\" /> the ratio of the homothety is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/d/e1d4a26db68f4b920424323be05ecc276209418a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k =  \\frac {\\vec PH}{\\vec OP} = 4 \\cos A \\cos B \\cos C.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"242\" height=\"47\" />\nWe recall that vertex of Kosnita triangle are:  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> is the circumcenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27829ed5d0fea089dbc523ed2e95a4c46d57a7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OBC, L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" /> is the circumcenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/4/444bc2c87ac5c335ba13fc88367cb1ece691b42a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OAB, M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" /> is the circumcenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/6/e461b49338c6511c27114775f8b514db02840513.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OAC,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is circumcenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/0/060b13a1e141783844c9df0e251553bd50eb1388.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><i><b>Proof</b></i>\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be orthocenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/1/c21aaa24354696abca7189beccdecd1640cbcf3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_0, Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" /> be the center of Nine-point circle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/b/0eba11bed189d2ae4f665f3a35ada1a5830a4213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_0, HQO$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" /> is the Euler line of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/0/060b13a1e141783844c9df0e251553bd50eb1388.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" />\nWell known that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is antiparallel <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> with respect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/f/52f7f053a3b7894bf50284280ba03a07d7d6f68a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A.$\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/1/0b1d8f246c1f2c2fbe6fea0847d28a9ab77e8338.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LM$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> is the bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/8/12868051b676f8e852a80e3ef8c20e5fda701458.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/1/0b1d8f246c1f2c2fbe6fea0847d28a9ab77e8338.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LM$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> is antiparallel <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> with respect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b1ac662f7ddbbce489953c8b7693848239564aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/5/5a592c579c4ff761ea5d6ab3908646b739482583.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies LM||EF.\\]\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" />\nSimilarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/1/681196b3b4873b066a3bb7236065609a578d6947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE||KL, DF||KM \\implies \\triangle DEF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"265\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/7/e870ab9a07760f98f7d89489b864a8231356e173.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle KLM$\" width=\"64\" height=\"13\" /> are homothetic.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the center of homothety.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />-excenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/0/390c2be2257492513aade0791c2bd7cb4a776d3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEF, O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" />-excenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/3/e23433e1df34281c20b0effef34d4863bb949690.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle KLM \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"111\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/b/a1b1bf1c52f5ea5b01dc8eb9472a4b60dfe4e05b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P \\in HO.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc5b43e3f21d53a0219814de27485d23efc41831.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = BC, \\alpha = \\angle A, \\beta = \\angle B, \\gamma = \\angle C, R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"296\" height=\"18\" /> circumradius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/919b9f77a6985e760286799909be5bfe0152f40e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/2/792065c8ff8b48e1f7e0aa68cd65859e1f7e9c2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle EHF = 180^\\circ - \\alpha, EF = BC |\\cos \\alpha| = 2R \\sin \\alpha |\\cos \\alpha|.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"440\" height=\"20\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/5/5451e550709eca210417f1662e7fbc9493e45167.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[LM = \\frac {R}{2} (\\tan \\beta + \\tan \\gamma) = \\frac {R \\sin (\\beta + \\gamma)}{2 \\cos \\beta \\cdot \\cos \\gamma} \\implies\\]\" width=\"359\" height=\"42\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/2/5a2c5f367c966c1398c9f69d4f42fa473cf87752.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k = \\frac {DE}{KL} = 4\\cos \\alpha \\cdot \\cos \\beta \\cdot \\cos \\gamma \\implies\\]\" width=\"284\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/7/1371129f8fe44d4f2052ab9efb04ace38b68ff92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {\\vec {PH}}{\\vec {OP}}= 4 \\cos A \\cos B \\cos C \\implies P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"267\" height=\"47\" /> is the point  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/8/638c7f739eb499fadd8b38c01c1197b0890d8ba0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X(24).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Theorem_3\">Theorem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Kimberling%E2%80%99s_point_X(24)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Theorem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:X24_as_Exeter.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/8/88/X24_as_Exeter.png/450px-X24_as_Exeter.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"450\" height=\"352\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/8/88/X24_as_Exeter.png/675px-X24_as_Exeter.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/8/88/X24_as_Exeter.png/900px-X24_as_Exeter.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> be the reference triangle (other than a right triangle). Let the altitudes through the vertices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/9/299ddf7c0f03ea46bf09f81f93adeea0756aa15c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B, C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"16\" /> meet the circumcircle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/d/ded21d28ee089ef0edfa210c35d1d473aa646d1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_0, B_0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/5/785508630245d8ce779145238803c538c53a7f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"24\" height=\"16\" /> respectively. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/2/022948689ac03ea1705a6af78b86d32ae2a369eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;B&#39;C&#39;$\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> be the triangle formed by the tangents at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/f/ccf6d387ce491c0ca100c134021f21f616d75162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/8/de82b5de37f029271b42d807a7a35ac5a7e8e7b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> (Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/1090530ae883b627e090bfb5e450ef796febca40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> be the vertex opposite to the side formed by the tangent at the vertex A). Prove that the lines through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb877bd52afc2e4cfd025de615082ad4dcfe9746.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_0A&#39;, B_0B&#39;,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/b/08b33e2e401ff3a3cb33dbe07332c71aca641ba8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_0C&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"19\" /> are concurrent, the point of concurrence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/3/653b5ceec5fba0e9db2ef680331111f16a298291.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X_{24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"17\" /> lies on Euler line of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/2/dd2e77a5a88ff7dc4c2347bb6bc4c0807334ca06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC,  X_{24} = O + \\frac {2}{J^2 + 1} (H – O), J = \\frac {|OH|}{R}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"345\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p><i><b>Proof</b></i>\n</p><p>At first one can prove that lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb877bd52afc2e4cfd025de615082ad4dcfe9746.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_0A&#39;, B_0B&#39;,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/b/08b33e2e401ff3a3cb33dbe07332c71aca641ba8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_0C&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"19\" /> are concurrent. This follows from the fact that lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/e/a8e18602e5460875af10e59b16828e13dedb28d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AA_0, BB_0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/1/371d03d750211ee0510a8a5c14dcbeb04c97477c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CC_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"33\" height=\"15\" /> are concurrent at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <i><b>Mapping theorem</b></i> (see Exeter point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/2/2a21e4cbdaecf2dc120047f0b423e78fbd7887cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X_{22}).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"43\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/b/20b5016493b0d7c21d955a96116263208b10c8a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1, B_1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70b97eb4ad6e4e7a5a97e2547d9ed6e965960d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> be the midpoints of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/8/2782ccf4ca9cf31227fb7efa5433ce62f2739f36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC, AC,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"67\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/4/d3431b737f3671c3c1d717f039984ff101e97404.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"32\" height=\"16\" /> respectively. \n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c58fadd5d028145551e7bf1c5cf41ea9026a205.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_2, B_2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/5/b65e6facfe122c182fe14d503aeace2c52a9739d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> be the midpoints of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/1/fa12b4933ad96b3fc644fae781167f7aef45d386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AH, BH,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/0/fd0a7235440e6e51d63865a9bb199193fbcc80d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CH,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> respectively.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/8/c58115f9f932e1110f7c223aa7df555996d65a16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_3, B_3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/85160260d550bf33be28c0a722237c3bc60e8c02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> be the foots of altitudes from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/f/ccf6d387ce491c0ca100c134021f21f616d75162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/7/737b15f20e17e7834a83b8188337bade510f22f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"17\" height=\"16\" /> respectively.\n</p><p>The points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/f/cef3dddec93db833889b0c976b4d8ced6a5c7fbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, A_2, H,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/1/791fe65c9d1ed7d8ed33a5025f40c5c7f9e476af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> are collinear. Similarly the points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/2/f925e332e5679c7ca4c2c931d3c05b7adfd6479f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B, B_2, H, B_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/e/8ae3ceaa0a52ea02326d5c5d17b8607c99f14b3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C, C_2, H, C_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" /> are collinear. \n</p><p>Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/e/22ec107d9afef9af9ebb250e7321724484a3f482.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_{\\Omega}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> the inversion with respect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/8/de82b5de37f029271b42d807a7a35ac5a7e8e7b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />  It is evident that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/2/2f2268b0c759ba4856b161f5661c70997b6e3c01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_{\\Omega}(A&#39;) = A_1,  I_{\\Omega}(B&#39;) = B_1, I_{\\Omega}(C&#39;) = C_1, I_{\\Omega}(A_0) = A_0, I_{\\Omega}(B_0) = B_0, I_{\\Omega}(C_0) = C_0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"632\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51d22c86f7b67bc5b1db8aaff4bfd6a158debb9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_A = I_{\\Omega}(A&#39;A_0), \\omega_B =  I_{\\Omega}(B&#39;B_0)  \\omega_C =  I_{\\Omega}(C&#39;C_0) \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"411\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/1/c7177ce8e5df8e7df9e249930e7889261c2d3453.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A_0 \\in \\omega_A, A_1 \\in \\omega_A, O \\in \\omega_A, B_0 \\in \\omega_B, B_1 \\in \\omega_B, O \\in \\omega_B \\implies\\ O = \\omega_A \\cap \\omega_B \\cap \\omega_C.\\]\" width=\"608\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>It is known that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/6/b466b4029a56f895c1ee1c4f2e16809366dd8bd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_2O = HA_1 = A_0A_1, A_2O || HA_1 \\implies \\angle OA_2A_0 = \\angle A_1A_0A_2, OA_1 ||A_0A_2 \\implies A_2 \\in \\omega_A.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"692\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/5/6b5eca7e89c0bdbf69ba6ff493871eb9dd1c84cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_2 \\in \\omega_B, C_2 \\in \\omega_C.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>We use <i><b>Claim</b></i> and get that the power of point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> with respect each circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/4/0145312ea8d28a0ec4169a7ae7b7235b2bf0788a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"10\" /> is \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/8/8d87393cf95ca4a0e4aa8cfb9d04ba31b42e765b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[HA_2 \\cdot HA_0 =  HB_2 \\cdot HB_0 = HC_2 \\cdot HC_0 = \\frac {R^2 \\cdot (1-J^2)} {2}.\\]\" width=\"443\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/f/7cffe2dd6965c912d99a5d804b447234628ecc80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H = AA_0 \\cap BB_0 \\cap CC_0 \\implies H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"255\" height=\"17\" /> lies on common radical axis of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/8/dd866c46173a1009337fc461405e13ce15be0890.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_A, \\omega_B,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/c/b3cd5d57cd4d2bf4d8189ea97403e7fb66dae53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_C.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"26\" height=\"10\" />\n</p><p>Therefore second crosspoint of these circles point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies on line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/b/e7b315b83c0b7c2f735f66c03cf870a83da077d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OH$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> which is the Euler line of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/0/ee0b3f67c82d03d07b6dbbe1220570cddf2f85f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"97\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/0/e30f8fa9774e24f08b91c7b32b88e8067a164652.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X_{24} = I_{\\Omega}(E)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"20\" /> lies on the same Euler line as desired.\n</p><p>Last we will find the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/2/0623c9b0dbd09752c5d4dd2eada893deaef907b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OX_{24}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/3/b53dc74f693cc50cc13df64f4daf1f25597012c2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[OH \\cdot HE = \\frac {R^2 \\cdot (1–J^2)} {2}.\\]\" width=\"193\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/a/f8aa1bdda98bebb1b0929e0b9e20721734e973a1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[OE \\cdot OX_{24} = (OH + HE)\\cdot OX_{24} = R^2.\\]\" width=\"313\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/a/97a35eb29a4f2448068d9d28e5c31638c77257fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {OX_{24}}{OH} =  \\frac {R^2}{OH^2 + OH \\cdot HE} = \\frac {1}{J^2 + \\frac {1– J^2} {2}} =  \\frac {2}{1+J^2},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"399\" height=\"48\" /> as desired. \n</p><p><i><b>Claim</b></i>\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AH_HF.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/25/AH_HF.png/400px-AH_HF.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"391\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/25/AH_HF.png/600px-AH_HF.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/2/25/AH_HF.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/a/91ae80de04ce313dba6efc4d1bbfd0881281429d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD, BE,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"70\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07d29465728e92952374a857beaee91665d8dbd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> be the heights of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/a/73a145c3439b525da2eb08e4320903ba8de93395.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC, H = AD \\cap BE \\cap CF.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"239\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/6/bf64abcf44788cd95e5bc12d19946f7f83481ad2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AH \\cdot HD = \\frac {R^2 (1 – J^2)}{2},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"184\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are circumradius and circumcenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/8/e58164868a13195e72d60d6df535c87c17418edd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC, J = \\frac {OH}{R}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"144\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><i><b>Proof</b></i>\n</p><p>It is known that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/f/71f400668c331c8c6d2eae01f5b76a9b9ec9e644.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC \\sim \\triangle AEF.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/0/2f0a7d7c258303059f47bdf06225530ab3bbdb1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = \\frac {AF} {AC} = \\cos A \\implies AH = 2 R k = 2 R \\cos A.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"367\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Similarly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/c/32c048b84953a4aa652c455440eee9fafef22c37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BH =  2 R \\cos B, DH = BH \\sin \\angle CBE = BH \\cos C = 2R \\cos B \\cos C.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"547\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/6/52632c67afd1afb621ba5f0c81ea024d07f61ad1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AH \\cdot HD = 4R^2 \\cos A \\cos B \\cos C.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"270\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/9/469883035296aee2178f6c0f3446dfe9575729e9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[J^2 = \\frac {HO^2}{R^2} = 1 – 8 \\cos A \\cos B \\cos C \\ \\implies AH \\cdot HD = \\frac {R^2 (1 – J^2)}{2}.\\]\" width=\"496\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018092643\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.066 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.082 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 799/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 35175/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:23135:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018092643 and revision id 182996. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}